- **`annassign` value extraction** (`lower-annassign`): detects `=` in the annassign kids and takes the last kid as the value; `x: T` (no `=`) lowers to `none`. Correct for the single-target grammar; subscript/attribute targets share `assign-sides`.
- **Refusal honesty**: unknown `\N{...}` names refuse with `"\N{…} unknown Unicode character name"`; malformed escapes (missing/absent brace) with `"malformed \N character escape"` — both name the construct honestly. (The *boundary* is honest; only the digit-name *content* is wrong, per finding 2.)
- **`py/make-exc` nil→empty-args change**: the two other callers (`py/gen-fail` at `:486`, the provenance constructor at `:1071`) pass non-nil messages or an exception instance; the bare-`raise` path is separate. The change is directionally CPython-correct (bare → `args = ()`), and the "every other caller passes a real message" claim holds.
